WEBVTT

00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:04.800
What the?!

00:02:52.633 --> 00:02:54.900
Okay, i think i found a way

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.900
We can bypass that
construction just east of here.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:03:00.067
We might even make pennsylvania
faster than we thought.

00:03:00.101 --> 00:03:01.501
Yeah.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.800
Problem is we're not
going to pennsylvania.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.834
Wait... what?

00:03:05.867 --> 00:03:08.267
I just got a call from an old friend.

00:03:08.301 --> 00:03:10.267
Her father was killed last night.

00:03:10.301 --> 00:03:11.800
She thinks it might
be our kind of thing.

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.000
What?

00:03:13.034 --> 00:03:14.434
Yeah, believe me,

00:03:14.468 --> 00:03:17.934
<i>She never would've called,
never, if she didn't need us.</i>

00:03:19.967 --> 00:03:21.900
Come on. You coming or what?

00:03:33.134 --> 00:03:35.633
By "old friend," you mean...

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.900
A friend that's not new.

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:39.134
Yeah, thanks.

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:42.468
So, her name's cassie, huh?

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.201
You never mentioned her.

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:46.267
Didn't i? No.

00:03:46.301 --> 00:03:48.934
Yeah, we went out. You
mean you dated someone?

00:03:48.967 --> 00:03:52.234
For more than one night?

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.900
Am i speaking a language
you're not getting here?

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.401
Dad and i were working
a job in athens, ohio.

00:03:57.434 --> 00:04:00.301
She was finishing up college.
We went out for a couple weeks.

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:01.934
And?

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:07.000
Look, it's terrible about her dad,

00:04:07.034 --> 00:04:09.667
But it kind of sounds like
a standard car accident.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.967
I'm not seeing how it
fits with what we do.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.201
Which, by the way, how
does she know what we do?

00:04:19.733 --> 00:04:22.667
You told her. You told her the secret.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.667
Our big family rule number one...

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.967
We do what we do and
we shut up about it.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.600
For a year and a half, i do
nothing but lie to jessica,

00:04:29.633 --> 00:04:32.301
And you go out with this
chick in ohio a couple of times

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.568
And you tell her everything?

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.600
Dean!

00:04:35.633 --> 00:04:37.600
Yeah, looks like.

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.234
Anderson: It's a
newspaper we put out here,

00:04:44.235 --> 00:04:46.067
Not a bulletin for the mayor's office.

00:04:46.101 --> 00:04:47.867
Get off your soapbox, jimmy.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.134
I'm urging a little discretion is all.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:53.234
No, i think you're telling
us what you want us to print

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.167
And what you want us to sit on.

00:04:55.201 --> 00:04:56.967
I know you're upset, cassie.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.600
I liked your dad a lot.

00:04:58.633 --> 00:05:02.000
But i think your grief
is clouding your judgment.

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.867
Two black people were killed
on the same stretch of road

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.667
In the same way in three weeks.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.468
Jimmy, you're too close to this.

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.900
Those guys were friends of yours.

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:16.301
Again, i'm very sorry for your loss.

00:05:25.733 --> 00:05:28.234
Dean.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:29.834
Hey, cassie.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.201
This is my brother, sam.

00:05:41.967 --> 00:05:43.568
I'm sorry about your dad.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.468
Yeah, me, too.

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:54.101
My mother's in pretty bad shape.

00:05:54.134 --> 00:05:55.767
I've been staying with her.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.267
I wish she wouldn't go off by herself.

00:05:58.301 --> 00:06:00.667
She's been snervous and frightened.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.301
She was worried about dad.

00:06:02.334 --> 00:06:03.667
Why?

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:04.700
He was scared.

00:06:04.733 --> 00:06:06.267
He was seeing things.

00:06:06.301 --> 00:06:07.568
Like what?

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.468
He swore he saw an awful-Looking
black truck following him.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:12.867
A truck? Who was the driver?

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.900
He didn't talk about a
driver, just the truck.

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:18.501
He said it would appear and disappear.

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:21.367
And in the accident,
dad's truck was dented

00:06:21.401 --> 00:06:24.501
Like it had been slammed
into by something big.

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:25.733
Thanks.

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:29.301
Now, you're sure this
dent wasn't there before?

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:31.367
He sold cars, always drove a new one.

00:06:31.401 --> 00:06:33.468
There wasn't a scratch on that thing.

00:06:33.501 --> 00:06:37.301
It had rained hard that night.
There was mud everywhere.

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:42.034
There was a distinct set of
muddy tracks from dad's car

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:45.101
Leading right...

00:06:45.134 --> 00:06:48.101
To the edge where he went over.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:52.334
One set of tracks... his.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:55.034
And the first person killed
was a friend of your father's?

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:56.468
Best friend... clayton solmes.

00:06:56.501 --> 00:06:58.201
They owned a car dealership together.

00:06:58.234 --> 00:07:02.101
Same thing... dent, no tracks.

00:07:02.134 --> 00:07:05.600
And the cops said exactly
what they said about dad...

00:07:05.633 --> 00:07:07.301
"He lost control of his car."

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:09.534
Can you think of why your father
and partner might be targets?

00:07:09.568 --> 00:07:11.000
No.

00:07:11.034 --> 00:07:13.034
You think this vanishing
truck ran him off the road?

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:16.767
When you say it aloud like that...

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:22.134
Listen, i'm a little skeptical
about this ghost stuff

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:24.667
Or whatever it is you guys are into.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.201
Skeptical.

00:07:26.234 --> 00:07:28.700
If i remember, i think
you said i was nuts.

00:07:28.733 --> 00:07:30.568
That was then.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.867
Hmm.

00:07:34.867 --> 00:07:37.468
I just know that i can't
explain what happened up there,

00:07:37.501 --> 00:07:39.167
So i called you.

00:07:40.733 --> 00:07:43.468
Mom. Where have you been?

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:47.534
I had no idea you'd
invited friends over.

00:07:47.568 --> 00:07:51.900
Mom, this is dean, a friend
of mine from... college,

00:07:51.934 --> 00:07:54.468
And his brother, sam.

00:07:54.501 --> 00:07:58.800
Well, l-L-L-I
won't interrupt you.

00:07:58.834 --> 00:08:00.067
Mrs. Robinson? Hmm?

00:08:00.101 --> 00:08:02.534
We're sorry for your loss.

00:08:02.568 --> 00:08:05.534
We'd like to talk to you for
a minute, if you don't mind.

00:08:05.568 --> 00:08:09.900
I'm really not up to that just now.

00:09:05.301 --> 00:09:07.900
Dd: Jimmy meant something to this town.

00:09:07.934 --> 00:09:09.633
He was one of our best.

00:09:09.667 --> 00:09:12.167
It won't be the same without him.

00:09:12.201 --> 00:09:15.134
Our best seem to be dropping like flies.

00:09:15.167 --> 00:09:17.000
Clayton, my father, jimmy.

00:09:17.034 --> 00:09:19.800
What is it exactly you want me to do?

00:09:19.834 --> 00:09:23.800
Well, how about closing this
section of road for starters?

00:09:23.834 --> 00:09:26.000
Close the main road, the
only road in and out of town?

00:09:26.034 --> 00:09:30.134
Accidents happen, cassie. That's
what they are... accidents.

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:32.568
Did the cops check for
denting on jimmy's car

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.234
To see if it was pushed?

00:09:34.267 --> 00:09:35.434
Who's this?

00:09:35.468 --> 00:09:38.401
Dean and sam winchester, family friends.

00:09:38.434 --> 00:09:41.568
This is mayor harold todd.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.767
There's one set of tracks...
one. Doesn't point to foul play.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:47.101
Mayor, the police and town officials

00:09:47.134 --> 00:09:48.867
Take their cues from you...
if you're indifferent about...

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.167
Indifferent?

00:09:50.201 --> 00:09:53.034
Would you close the road
if the victims were white?

00:09:53.067 --> 00:09:55.867
You're suggesting i'm racist, cassie.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:59.434
I'm the last person you
should talk to like that.

00:09:59.468 --> 00:10:00.434
Why is that?

00:10:00.468 --> 00:10:02.667
Why don't you k your mother?

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:11.534
I'll say this for her... she's fearless.

00:10:11.568 --> 00:10:12.600
Mm-Hmm.

00:10:12.633 --> 00:10:16.134
Bet she kicked your ass a coupleimes.

00:10:16.167 --> 00:10:19.800
What's interesting is you guys
never really look at each other

00:10:19.834 --> 00:10:20.934
At the same time.

00:10:20.967 --> 00:10:23.401
You look at her when she's not looking.

00:10:23.434 --> 00:10:25.834
She checks you out when you look away.

00:10:27.367 --> 00:10:31.201
It's just a... just an
interesting observation

00:10:31.234 --> 00:10:34.834
In a, you know,
observationally interesting way.

00:10:34.867 --> 00:10:37.568
You think we might have some
more pressing issues here?

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.900
Hey, if i'm hitting a nerve...

00:10:39.934 --> 00:10:41.234
Oh, let's go.

00:10:56.201 --> 00:10:58.401
Excuse me. Are you ron stubbins?

00:10:58.434 --> 00:11:00.234
Friends with jimmy anderson?

00:11:00.267 --> 00:11:01.434
Who are you?

00:11:01.468 --> 00:11:04.067
We're with mr. Anderson's
insurance company.

00:11:04.101 --> 00:11:06.900
Just here to dot some
i's and cross some t's.

00:11:06.934 --> 00:11:09.201
We were just wondering,
had the deceased mentioned

00:11:09.234 --> 00:11:10.767
Any unusual recent experiences?

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.234
What do you mean, "unusual"?

00:11:12.267 --> 00:11:14.067
Well, visions, hallucinations.

00:11:14.101 --> 00:11:17.000
It's all part of a medical
examination kind of thing.

00:11:17.034 --> 00:11:19.101
What company you say you were with?

00:11:19.134 --> 00:11:21.434
All tional mutual.

00:11:21.468 --> 00:11:25.034
Tell me, did he ever
mention seeing a truck,

00:11:25.067 --> 00:11:27.034
A big black truck?

00:11:27.067 --> 00:11:29.434
What the hell you talking
about? You even speaking english?

00:11:29.468 --> 00:11:32.867
Son, this truck, a big,
scary, monster-Looking thing?

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.568
Yeah, actually, i think so.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:36.633
Hmm.

00:11:36.667 --> 00:11:38.301
What?

00:11:38.334 --> 00:11:39.934
I have heard of a truck like that.

00:11:39.967 --> 00:11:41.234
You have?

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:42.267
Where?

00:11:42.301 --> 00:11:44.434
Not where... when.

00:11:44.468 --> 00:11:47.800
Back in the '60s, there
was a string of deaths.

00:11:47.834 --> 00:11:50.201
Black men.

00:11:50.234 --> 00:11:54.534
Stores they disappeared in
a big, nasty black truck.

00:11:54.568 --> 00:11:56.067
They ever catch the guy who did it?

00:11:56.101 --> 00:11:57.134
Never found him.

00:11:57.167 --> 00:12:01.800
Hell, not sure they even really looked.

00:12:01.834 --> 00:12:04.000
See, there was a time

00:12:04.034 --> 00:12:10.867
This town wasn't too
friendly to all its citizens.

00:12:13.234 --> 00:12:14.301
Thank you.

00:12:19.101 --> 00:12:20.101
Truck.

00:12:20.134 --> 00:12:21.568
Keeps coming up, doesn't it?

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.834
<i>I was thinking. You heard
of the flying dutchman?</i>

00:12:23.867 --> 00:12:26.468
Yeah, a ghost ship infused
with the captain's evil spirit.

00:12:26.501 --> 00:12:28.034
It was basically a part of him.

00:12:28.067 --> 00:12:30.201
So, what if we're dealing
with the same thing?

00:12:30.234 --> 00:12:33.000
A phantom truck who's the
extension of some bastard ghost,

00:12:33.034 --> 00:12:34.201
Re-Enacting past crimes.

00:12:34.234 --> 00:12:36.067
The victims have all been black men.

00:12:36.101 --> 00:12:37.600
I think it's more than that.

00:12:37.633 --> 00:12:40.401
They all seem connected
to cassie and her family.

00:12:40.434 --> 00:12:42.600
All right, well, you work that angle.

00:12:42.633 --> 00:12:43.667
Go talk to her.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:44.934
Yeah, i will.

00:12:44.967 --> 00:12:47.201
Oh, and you might also want
to mention that other thing.

00:12:47.234 --> 00:12:49.767
What other thing?

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.733
That serious unfinished business.

00:12:52.767 --> 00:12:56.367
Dean, what is going on between you two?

00:12:56.401 --> 00:12:58.834
So maybe we were a little
bit more involved than i said.

00:12:58.867 --> 00:13:01.834
Oh, okay, yeah.

00:13:01.867 --> 00:13:03.900
Okay, a lot more... maybe.

00:13:03.934 --> 00:13:07.034
I told her the secret about
what we do, and i shouldn't have.

00:13:07.067 --> 00:13:10.034
Look, man, everybody's got to
open up to someone sometime.

00:13:10.067 --> 00:13:11.334
Yeah, i don't.

00:13:11.367 --> 00:13:14.600
It was stupid to get that
close. I mean, look how it ended.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.600
Would you stop?

00:13:19.501 --> 00:13:21.468
Blink or something.

00:13:21.501 --> 00:13:23.067
You loved her.

00:13:23.101 --> 00:13:24.234
Oh, god.

00:13:24.267 --> 00:13:28.800
You were in love with
her, but you dumped her.

00:13:31.201 --> 00:13:33.767
Oh, wow.

00:13:35.501 --> 00:13:36.867
She dumped you.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:39.700
Get in the car.

00:13:39.733 --> 00:13:41.834
Get in the car!

00:13:57.034 --> 00:13:58.367
Dean.

00:13:58.401 --> 00:13:59.934
Hey. Hey.

00:13:59.967 --> 00:14:02.101
Come on in.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.834
So, you busy?

00:14:07.867 --> 00:14:09.367
The paper is doing a tribute to jimmy.

00:14:09.401 --> 00:14:14.401
I was just going through
his stuff, his awards,

00:14:14.434 --> 00:14:17.334
Trying to find the words.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.167
That's got to be tough.

00:14:21.201 --> 00:14:23.600
For years this family owned
the paper, the dorians.

00:14:23.633 --> 00:14:25.600
They had a whites-Only staff policy.

00:14:25.633 --> 00:14:29.534
After they sold it, jimmy
became the first black reporter.

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:32.401
He became editor.

00:14:32.434 --> 00:14:34.568
He taught me everything.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.034
Where's your brother?

00:14:37.834 --> 00:14:39.134
Not here.

00:14:39.167 --> 00:14:41.334
All right, so, what brings you here?

00:14:41.367 --> 00:14:43.401
I'm trying to find the connection

00:14:43.434 --> 00:14:44.934
Between the three victims.

00:14:44.967 --> 00:14:46.434
By the way, did you talk to your mom

00:14:46.468 --> 00:14:48.501
About what todd said
about not being a racist?

00:14:48.534 --> 00:14:49.700
I did.

00:14:49.733 --> 00:14:53.000
She didn't want to talk about it.

00:14:55.534 --> 00:14:59.167
So, just then, why did you
ask where my brother was?

00:14:59.201 --> 00:15:00.600
Nothing. Not important.

00:15:00.633 --> 00:15:03.633
Could it be because without
him here it'just you and me

00:15:03.667 --> 00:15:05.501
And not you, me, and sam,
which would be easier?

00:15:05.534 --> 00:15:06.800
It's not easier.

00:15:06.834 --> 00:15:08.501
Look...

00:15:08.534 --> 00:15:11.234
No, forget it. It's fine.

00:15:11.267 --> 00:15:14.301
Keep it strictly business.

00:15:14.334 --> 00:15:16.800
I forgot you do that.

00:15:16.834 --> 00:15:19.367
Do what?

00:15:19.401 --> 00:15:21.767
Oh, whenever we get...

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:24.034
What's the word, close?...

00:15:24.067 --> 00:15:26.834
Anywhere in the neighborhood
of emotional vulnerability,

00:15:26.867 --> 00:15:29.267
You back off or make some joke

00:15:29.301 --> 00:15:31.301
Or find any way to shut the door on me.

00:15:31.334 --> 00:15:33.234
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:15:33.267 --> 00:15:36.034
See, i'm not the one who
took that big, final door

00:15:36.067 --> 00:15:37.867
And slammed it behind
me, and i'm not the one

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.367
Who took the key and buried it.

00:15:39.401 --> 00:15:41.101
Are we done with this metaphor?

00:15:41.134 --> 00:15:42.733
All i'm saying is i was totally
up front with you back then

00:15:42.767 --> 00:15:43.800
And you nailed me with it.

00:15:43.834 --> 00:15:45.767
The guy i'm hoping might be in my future

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.700
Tells me he professionally pops ghosts.

00:15:47.733 --> 00:15:49.134
Those weren't the words i used.

00:15:49.167 --> 00:15:51.334
And he has to leave too
work with his father. I did.

00:15:51.367 --> 00:15:53.000
All i could think was,
if you want out, fine.

00:15:53.034 --> 00:15:54.967
But don't tell me this insane story.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.401
It was the truth, cassie,

00:15:56.434 --> 00:15:58.900
It didn't sound so insane the
minute you thought i could help.

00:15:58.934 --> 00:16:01.000
Back then i thought you
just wanted to dump me.

00:16:01.034 --> 00:16:03.800
Whoa, let's not forget
who dumped who, okay?

00:16:03.834 --> 00:16:06.000
I thought it was what you wanted.

00:16:06.034 --> 00:16:07.134
Well, it wasn't.

00:16:07.167 --> 00:16:08.967
I didn't mean to hurt you.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:09.967
Well, you did.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.934
I'm sorry. Yeah, me, too.

00:18:14.367 --> 00:18:17.000
Absolutely.

00:18:17.033 --> 00:18:20.033
Actually, we were always
pretty good at fighting.

00:18:20.067 --> 00:18:22.534
This, we were good at.

00:18:22.567 --> 00:18:26.900
It's all the other stuff, not so much.

00:18:26.933 --> 00:18:29.667
Hey, i tried.

00:18:29.701 --> 00:18:33.734
I told you who i really was.
It was a big first for me.

00:18:33.768 --> 00:18:35.933
Why'd you tell me?

00:18:35.967 --> 00:18:38.367
I don't know.

00:18:41.367 --> 00:18:44.701
I guess i couldn't lie to you.

00:18:47.501 --> 00:18:49.567
Dean...

00:18:49.601 --> 00:18:53.134
When you told me that story,

00:18:53.167 --> 00:18:54.933
It scared the hell out of me.

00:18:54.967 --> 00:18:59.300
I thought you were nuts, dangerous even.

00:18:59.334 --> 00:19:02.933
Actually...

00:19:02.967 --> 00:19:07.267
Maybe i was looking for
a reason to walk away.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:13.000
In my work i see some horrible things,

00:19:13.033 --> 00:19:15.768
Things that can't be explained.

00:19:15.801 --> 00:19:17.200
I deal with them.

00:19:17.234 --> 00:19:19.834
But working things out with you?

00:19:19.868 --> 00:19:22.501
I'm a scary one, all right.

00:19:22.534 --> 00:19:24.067
Hmm.

00:19:29.834 --> 00:19:34.434
Well, usually thgs get worked out

00:19:34.467 --> 00:19:37.234
When you really want them to.

00:19:41.534 --> 00:19:45.900
Yeah, but i'm still really
involved in my dad's work.

00:19:48.067 --> 00:19:53.601
No more excuses, okay? From you or me.

00:19:53.634 --> 00:19:54.834
Okay.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.900
Yeah

00:20:14.933 --> 00:20:18.033
You're kidding.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.768
And he's with me.

00:20:25.768 --> 00:20:28.033
Where were you last night?

00:20:28.067 --> 00:20:31.067
You didn't make it back to the motel.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:32.200
Nope.

00:20:32.234 --> 00:20:34.167
I'm guessing you guys worked things out.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:36.200
We'll be working things
out when we're 90.

00:20:36.234 --> 00:20:37.501
So, what happened?

00:20:37.534 --> 00:20:39.834
Every bone crushed, internal
organs turned to pudding.

00:20:39.868 --> 00:20:41.067
The cops are all stumped,

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:42.967
But it's almost like
something ran him over.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.534
Something like a truck? Yep.

00:20:44.567 --> 00:20:46.634
Tracks? Nope.

00:20:46.667 --> 00:20:48.734
What was the mayor doing here anyway?

00:20:48.768 --> 00:20:51.200
He owned the property.
Bought it a few weeks ago.

00:20:51.234 --> 00:20:53.367
Yeah, but he's white.
Doesn't fit the pattern.

00:20:53.401 --> 00:20:55.234
Killings didn't happen up on the road.

00:20:55.267 --> 00:20:58.134
That doesn't fit, either.

00:21:04.067 --> 00:21:05.334
Thanks.

00:21:05.367 --> 00:21:07.701
I'm trying to find some
link between those killings

00:21:07.734 --> 00:21:09.501
In the '60s and what's going on now.

00:21:09.534 --> 00:21:11.467
There wasn't a lot
about it in the paper.

00:21:11.501 --> 00:21:14.334
Not surprising. Probably
minimal-Police-Work deal.

00:21:14.367 --> 00:21:16.667
Back then, equal justice under the law

00:21:16.701 --> 00:21:18.601
Wasn't too literal around here.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:22.367
Yeah?

00:21:22.401 --> 00:21:23.933
Sam: Okay, the courthouse records

00:21:23.967 --> 00:21:27.100
Show that mr. And mrs. Mayor
bought an abandoned property.

00:21:27.134 --> 00:21:29.100
The previous owner
was the dorian family,

00:21:29.134 --> 00:21:30.534
For like 150 years.

00:21:30.567 --> 00:21:31.868
Dorian? Yeah.

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:34.300
Didn't you say the dorian
family used to own this paper?

00:21:34.334 --> 00:21:36.300
Along with most everything
else around here.

00:21:36.334 --> 00:21:38.467
Real pillars of the town.

00:21:38.501 --> 00:21:39.768
Right, right.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:43.734
That's interesting.

00:21:43.768 --> 00:21:45.701
What?

00:21:45.734 --> 00:21:48.801
This cyrus dorian, he
vanished in april of '63.

00:21:48.834 --> 00:21:51.801
The case was investigated
but never solved.

00:21:51.834 --> 00:21:54.167
It was the time the string
of murders was going on.

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:55.868
Well, i pulled a bunch of
paper up on the dorian place.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:57.567
It must've been in bad shape
when the mayor bought it.

00:21:57.601 --> 00:21:59.100
Why is that?

00:21:59.134 --> 00:22:00.801
The first thing he did
was bulldoze the place.

00:22:00.834 --> 00:22:03.501
Mayor todd knocked down the dorianlace?

00:22:03.534 --> 00:22:07.200
It was a big deal. One of
the oldest local houses left.

00:22:07.234 --> 00:22:08.801
It made the front page.

00:22:08.834 --> 00:22:09.967
You got a date?

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:13.267
Uh... the 3rd of last month.

00:22:17.467 --> 00:22:20.933
Mayor todd bulldozed the
dorian family home on the 3rd.

00:22:20.967 --> 00:22:23.834
The first killing was the very next day.

00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:47.768
Dean!

00:23:51.980 --> 00:23:54.047
Maybe you could throw
a couple shots in that.

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:58.714
You didn't see who
was driving the truck?

00:24:00.114 --> 00:24:01.514
It seemed to be no one.

00:24:04.413 --> 00:24:06.614
Everything was moving so fast.

00:24:08.317 --> 00:24:13.617
And then it was just gone.
Why didn't it kill us?

00:24:13.651 --> 00:24:17.317
Whatever is controlling the
truck wants you afraid first.

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:22.517
Mrs. Robinson, cassie said
that your husband saw the truck

00:24:22.551 --> 00:24:25.183
Before he died.

00:24:25.217 --> 00:24:26.517
Mom?

00:24:26.551 --> 00:24:28.018
Hmm?

00:24:28.984 --> 00:24:31.851
Martin was under a lot of stress.

00:24:31.884 --> 00:24:33.851
You can't be sure about
what he was seeing.

00:24:33.884 --> 00:24:36.250
Well, after tonight i think
we can be reasonably sure

00:24:36.284 --> 00:24:37.651
That he was seeing a truck.

00:24:37.684 --> 00:24:42.984
What happened tonight, you
and cassie are marked, okay?

00:24:43.018 --> 00:24:45.350
Your daughter could die,
so if you know something,

00:24:45.384 --> 00:24:47.317
Now would be a really good
time to tell us about it.

00:24:47.350 --> 00:24:49.217
Dean... yes.

00:24:49.250 --> 00:24:51.918
Yes, he said he saw a truck.

00:24:51.951 --> 00:24:54.150
Did he know who it belonged to?

00:24:54.183 --> 00:24:56.484
He thought he did. Who was that?

00:24:58.551 --> 00:25:01.517
Cyrus...

00:25:01.551 --> 00:25:04.617
A man named cyrus.

00:25:07.951 --> 00:25:10.350
Is this cyrus?

00:25:10.384 --> 00:25:15.984
Cyrus dorian died
more than 40 years ago.

00:25:16.018 --> 00:25:20.284
How do you know he died, mrs. Robinson?

00:25:21.984 --> 00:25:24.183
The paper said he went missing.

00:25:24.217 --> 00:25:26.551
How do you know he died?

00:25:26.584 --> 00:25:30.217
We were all very young.

00:25:32.217 --> 00:25:35.083
I dated cyrus a while.

00:25:35.117 --> 00:25:38.183
I was also seeing martin,
in secret of course

00:25:38.217 --> 00:25:44.450
'Cause interracial couples
didn't go over too well then.

00:25:44.484 --> 00:25:46.984
When i broke it off with cyrus,

00:25:47.018 --> 00:25:49.918
And when he found out about martin...

00:25:49.951 --> 00:25:55.417
I don't know... he changed.

00:25:55.450 --> 00:26:01.250
His hatred... his
hatred was frightening.

00:26:01.284 --> 00:26:02.751
The string of murders.

00:26:02.784 --> 00:26:05.250
There were rumors,

00:26:05.284 --> 00:26:08.117
People of color disappearing
into some kind oa truck.

00:26:11.484 --> 00:26:14.217
Nothing was ever done.

00:26:19.517 --> 00:26:21.417
Martin and...

00:26:23.417 --> 00:26:27.717
Martin and i, we were gonna be married

00:26:27.751 --> 00:26:29.751
In that little church near here,

00:26:29.784 --> 00:26:32.684
But last minute, we decided to elope

00:26:32.717 --> 00:26:35.018
'Cause we didn't want all the attention.

00:26:35.050 --> 00:26:36.284
And cyrus?

00:26:43.018 --> 00:26:48.317
The day we set for the wedding

00:26:48.350 --> 00:26:53.884
Was the day someone
set fire to the church.

00:27:01.984 --> 00:27:07.183
There was a children's
choir practicing in there.

00:27:09.651 --> 00:27:12.784
They all died.

00:27:15.217 --> 00:27:17.784
Did the attacks stop after that?

00:27:17.817 --> 00:27:20.751
No, there was one more.

00:27:22.751 --> 00:27:27.551
One night that truck came for martin.

00:27:30.018 --> 00:27:32.484
Cyrus beat him something terrible,

00:27:37.183 --> 00:27:40.384
But martin... you see, martin got loose

00:27:40.417 --> 00:27:43.250
And he started hitting cyrus

00:27:43.284 --> 00:27:47.484
And he just kept hitting
him and hitting him.

00:27:58.751 --> 00:28:01.083
Why didn't you call the cops?

00:28:05.417 --> 00:28:08.617
This was 40 years ago.

00:28:08.651 --> 00:28:12.250
He called on his friends...

00:28:12.284 --> 00:28:14.217
Clayton, solmes, and jimmy anderson...

00:28:14.250 --> 00:28:17.584
And they put cyrus' body into the truck

00:28:17.617 --> 00:28:22.183
And then rolled it into the
swamp at the edge of his land

00:28:22.217 --> 00:28:28.717
And all three of them kept
that secret all these years.

00:28:30.751 --> 00:28:32.183
And now all three are gone.

00:28:32.217 --> 00:28:33.317
So is mayor todd.

00:28:35.083 --> 00:28:38.384
Now, he said that you of all people

00:28:38.417 --> 00:28:40.217
Would know that he is not a racist.

00:28:40.250 --> 00:28:41.284
Why would he say that?

00:28:41.317 --> 00:28:42.317
He was a good man.

00:28:42.350 --> 00:28:45.617
He was a young deputy back then,

00:28:45.651 --> 00:28:47.384
Investigating cyrus's disappearance.

00:28:47.417 --> 00:28:53.117
Once he figured out what
martin and the others had done,

00:28:53.150 --> 00:28:58.951
He he did nothing

00:29:00.617 --> 00:29:03.684
Because he also knew
what cyrus had done.

00:29:06.817 --> 00:29:08.484
Why didn't you tell me?

00:29:08.517 --> 00:29:11.183
I thought i was protecting them.

00:29:13.250 --> 00:29:18.350
And now there's no one left to protect.

00:29:18.384 --> 00:29:19.751
Yes, there is.

00:29:29.018 --> 00:29:31.117
Oh, my life was so simple.

00:29:31.150 --> 00:29:35.617
Just school, exams,

00:29:35.651 --> 00:29:39.150
Papers on polycentric cultural norms.

00:29:39.183 --> 00:29:43.083
So i guess i saved you
from a boring existence.

00:29:43.117 --> 00:29:45.284
Occasionally i miss boring.

00:29:47.050 --> 00:29:48.617
So, this killer truck...

00:29:48.651 --> 00:29:52.517
I miss conversations that didn't
start with "this killer truck."

00:29:52.551 --> 00:29:54.984
Ah...

00:29:55.018 --> 00:29:56.951
All right, well, this cyrus guy,

00:29:56.984 --> 00:29:59.617
Evil on a level that
infected even his truck.

00:29:59.651 --> 00:30:03.150
When he died, the swamp became his tomb

00:30:03.183 --> 00:30:05.517
And his spirit was dormant for 40 years.

00:30:05.551 --> 00:30:06.751
So, what woke it up?

00:30:06.784 --> 00:30:09.350
The construction on his
house or the destructi.

00:30:09.384 --> 00:30:10.484
Right.

00:30:10.517 --> 00:30:13.284
Demolition or remodeling
can awaken spirits,

00:30:13.317 --> 00:30:15.018
Make them restless.

00:30:15.050 --> 00:30:17.417
Like that theater in illinois.

00:30:17.450 --> 00:30:18.684
Yeah.

00:30:18.717 --> 00:30:20.717
And the guy who tears
down the family homestead,

00:30:20.751 --> 00:30:23.250
Harold todd, is the same guy

00:30:23.284 --> 00:30:26.817
That kept cyrus's murder
quiet and unsolved.

00:30:26.851 --> 00:30:29.018
So now his spirit is
awakened and out for blood.

00:30:29.050 --> 00:30:31.317
I guess. Who knows what
ghosts are thinking anyway.

00:30:31.350 --> 00:30:34.717
You know we're gonna have to
dredge that body from the swamp?

00:30:34.751 --> 00:30:36.350
Maman.

00:30:36.384 --> 00:30:38.717
You said it. Yeah.

00:30:38.751 --> 00:30:39.717
Hey.

00:30:39.751 --> 00:30:40.717
Hey.

00:30:40.751 --> 00:30:42.784
She's asleep.

00:30:42.817 --> 00:30:44.884
Now what?

00:30:44.918 --> 00:30:46.617
You stay put and look after her.

00:30:46.651 --> 00:30:48.717
And we'll be back.
Don't leave the house.

00:30:48.751 --> 00:30:50.951
Don't go getting all
authoritative on me.

00:30:50.984 --> 00:30:52.050
I hate it.

00:30:53.484 --> 00:30:56.217
Don't leave the house, please?

00:31:08.183 --> 00:31:10.918
You coming or what?

00:31:15.517 --> 00:31:19.117
Sam: All right, let's get her up.

00:31:20.684 --> 00:31:23.918
All right. Little more.

00:31:23.951 --> 00:31:25.183
Little more.

00:31:26.450 --> 00:31:28.651
Litt more.

00:31:28.684 --> 00:31:29.918
All right, stop.

00:31:38.551 --> 00:31:39.684
Nice.

00:31:39.717 --> 00:31:41.784
Hell yeah.

00:31:41.817 --> 00:31:43.183
Now i know what she sees in you.

00:31:43.217 --> 00:31:44.450
What?

00:31:44.484 --> 00:31:47.018
Come on, you can admit it.
You're still in love with her.

00:31:47.050 --> 00:31:48.317
Can we focus, please?

00:31:48.350 --> 00:31:50.183
I'm just saying, dean.

00:31:50.217 --> 00:31:51.217
Hold that.

00:31:51.250 --> 00:31:53.851
All right. What am i getting?

00:31:53.884 --> 00:31:55.450
Gas, flashlight. Got it, got it.

00:31:55.484 --> 00:31:56.984
All right, let's get this done.

00:31:57.018 --> 00:31:59.250
All right. Got it.

00:32:16.551 --> 00:32:18.083
All right, let's get to it.

00:32:33.651 --> 00:32:36.250
Think that'll do it?

00:32:42.083 --> 00:32:44.050
I guess not.

00:32:47.677 --> 00:32:49.577
So burning the body had
no effect on that thing?

00:32:49.610 --> 00:32:50.944
Sure it did. Now it's really pissed.

00:32:50.977 --> 00:32:52.910
But cyrus's ghost is gone, right, dean?

00:32:52.944 --> 00:32:54.710
Apparently not the part
that's fused with the truck.

00:32:54.984 --> 00:32:56.783
Where you going?

00:32:56.817 --> 00:32:59.184
Going for a little ride.
Gonna lead that thing away.

00:32:59.217 --> 00:33:01.017
That rusted piece of
crap, you got to burn it.

00:33:01.050 --> 00:33:02.651
How the hell am i supposed
to burn a truck, dean?

00:33:02.684 --> 00:33:04.517
I don't know. Figure something out.

00:33:04.891 --> 00:33:06.524
Figure something...

00:33:46.421 --> 00:33:48.588
Hey, you got to give me a minute.

00:33:48.620 --> 00:33:50.121
I don't have a minute!
What are we doing?!

00:33:50.154 --> 00:33:53.121
Uh... let me get back to you.

00:33:55.588 --> 00:33:57.121
Hey, cassie? Hey, it's sam.

00:33:57.154 --> 00:34:00.187
Okay, i need some information
and it has to be exactly right.

00:34:03.454 --> 00:34:05.154
All right, dean. This better be good!

00:34:05.187 --> 00:34:08.787
Where are you? I'm in the middle of
nowhere with a killer truck on my ass!

00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:11.020
It's like it knows i
put the torch to cyrus!

00:34:11.054 --> 00:34:12.720
Dean, listen to me. It's important.

00:34:12.753 --> 00:34:13.820
I have to know exactly where you are.

00:34:13.854 --> 00:34:16.254
Decatur road, about two
miles off the highway.

00:34:16.287 --> 00:34:18.054
Okay, headed east? Yes!

00:34:22.987 --> 00:34:26.187
Oh, you son of a bitch.

00:34:26.221 --> 00:34:27.454
Okay, uh, turn right.

00:34:34.454 --> 00:34:35.653
You make the turn?

00:34:35.687 --> 00:34:37.087
Yeah, i made the turn!

00:34:37.121 --> 00:34:38.854
Move this thing along a little faster!

00:34:38.887 --> 00:34:40.454
All right, you see a road up ahead?

00:34:40.488 --> 00:34:41.687
No!

00:34:41.720 --> 00:34:43.454
Wait, yes, i see it!

00:34:43.488 --> 00:34:45.087
Okay, turn left. What?!

00:34:52.588 --> 00:34:54.154
All right, now what?

00:34:54.187 --> 00:34:56.154
Go exactly 7/10ths of a mile and stop.

00:34:56.187 --> 00:34:58.854
Stop? Exactly 7/10ths, dean.

00:34:58.887 --> 00:35:01.254
7/10ths, 7/10ths.

00:35:30.720 --> 00:35:33.554
Dean, are you still there?

00:35:33.588 --> 00:35:35.254
Yeah. What's happening?

00:35:35.287 --> 00:35:37.254
It's just staring at me. What do i do?

00:35:37.287 --> 00:35:39.653
Just what you are doing...
bringing it to you.

00:35:39.687 --> 00:35:40.753
Wh...

00:35:57.820 --> 00:35:59.354
Come on, come on.

00:36:19.387 --> 00:36:22.054
Dean?

00:36:22.087 --> 00:36:23.287
You still there?

00:36:23.321 --> 00:36:26.154
Dean?

00:36:26.187 --> 00:36:28.588
Where'd it go?

00:36:28.620 --> 00:36:31.820
Dean, you're where the church was.

00:36:31.854 --> 00:36:33.087
What church?

00:36:33.121 --> 00:36:35.588
The place cyrus burned down
and murdered all those kids.

00:36:35.620 --> 00:36:37.221
There's not a whole lot left.

00:36:37.254 --> 00:36:38.954
Church ground is hallowed ground

00:36:38.987 --> 00:36:40.488
Whether the church
is still there or not.

00:36:40.521 --> 00:36:42.554
Evil spirits cross over hallowed ground,

00:36:42.588 --> 00:36:44.321
Sometimes they're destroyed.

00:36:44.354 --> 00:36:49.254
So i figured maybe that
would get rid of it.

00:36:49.287 --> 00:36:50.287
Maybe?

00:36:50.321 --> 00:36:51.620
Maybe?!

00:36:51.653 --> 00:36:54.354
What if you were wrong?!

00:36:56.121 --> 00:36:58.820
Honestly, that thought
hadn't occurred to me.

00:37:03.020 --> 00:37:05.321
"Well, that honestly
didn't occur to me."

00:37:11.321 --> 00:37:12.987
I'm gonna kill him.

00:37:19.974 --> 00:37:23.007
My mother says to tell you thanks again.

00:37:27.940 --> 00:37:30.841
This was a better goodbye
than the last time.

00:37:30.874 --> 00:37:32.808
Yeah, well, maybe this time

00:37:32.841 --> 00:37:35.107
It'll be a little less permanent.

00:37:35.140 --> 00:37:38.707
You know what?

00:37:38.741 --> 00:37:41.741
I'm a realist.

00:37:41.774 --> 00:37:44.707
I don't see much hope for us, dean.

00:37:48.374 --> 00:37:51.240
Well, i've seen stranger things happen.

00:37:51.274 --> 00:37:52.940
Hell of a lot stranger.

00:37:57.607 --> 00:37:59.474
Goodbye, dean.

00:37:59.507 --> 00:38:02.474
I'll see you, cassie.

00:38:02.507 --> 00:38:05.441
I will.

00:38:58.007 --> 00:39:00.107
I like her.

00:39:00.140 --> 00:39:01.474
Yeah.

00:39:03.808 --> 00:39:05.574
You meet someone like her,

00:39:05.607 --> 00:39:08.407
Ever make you wonder if it's worth it...

00:39:08.441 --> 00:39:12.541
Putting everything else
on hold, doing what we do?

00:39:25.107 --> 00:39:28.207
Why don't you wake me up
when it's my turn to drive?



00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
